# Network blocks

Add blocks by mirroring a small neighbor (e.g. `MLPBlock` in `monai/networks/blocks/mlp.py`). Load only that neighbor plus, if you need dimension-aware layers, `monai/networks/blocks/aspp.py`.

## Class

- Subclass `torch.nn.Module`; call `super().__init__()` first; validate args early with `ValueError`.
- Support 2D and 3D via `spatial_dims`. Build dimension-aware layers with the MONAI factory `Conv[Conv.CONV, spatial_dims]` (from `monai.networks.layers.factories`) or `get_conv_layer` / `get_norm_layer`.
- Channel-first tensors: `(B, C, H, W[, D])`. Per-channel params broadcast with shape `(1, C, *[1]*spatial_dims)`.
- Implement `forward(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor`.

## Register (new file needs its own import line)

- Create `monai/networks/blocks/<name>.py`, then add `from .<name> import <Class>` to `monai/networks/blocks/__init__.py` (alphabetical by module name). Blocks are accessed via `from monai.networks.blocks import <Class>` — `monai/networks/__init__.py` does NOT re-export blocks.

## Always

- Apache header; `from __future__ import annotations`; Google docstrings; American English.
- Tests must cover 2D and 3D shapes; run under `eval_mode`.

Full skeleton + named neighbor: `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/networks.md`.

**Source of truth:** `monai/networks/blocks/mlp.py`, `monai/networks/blocks/aspp.py`, `monai/networks/blocks/__init__.py`, `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/networks.md`
